# Copy to .env.local and fill in, or run `vercel env pull .env.local` in docs/ (project persona-docs; a pull replaces the whole file). The docs need one secret: model access for "Ask AI". Every other part of the site works without it.

# === Ask AI: model access through Vercel AI Gateway ===
# `vercel env pull .env.local` writes a short-lived VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN of the persona-docs project; re-run it when it expires (about 12 hours).
# On Vercel, the project's own OIDC token covers it, so the deployed site needs nothing here.
VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN=
# Or a gateway key instead, which does not expire:
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# === Optional: the docs' public origin, for social cards and canonical URLs. Without it: https://docs.usepersona.dev ===
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DOCS_URL=

# === PostHog: product analytics, errors and replays (one project shared by the webapp, the landing and the docs; the host is a managed reverse proxy, so ad blockers do not drop events; leave the key empty to send nothing) ===
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=
